[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5601626435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321#issuecomment-5601626435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123321","id":5601626435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTeIJQw","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T12:12:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T12:12:25Z","body":"What's your suggestion for dealing with exported variables where you need to set the value in the setter to a property of a child node but the engine is calling the setter before the node and its children is ready?\r\n\r\nThis is common when making a custom control that contains children. I have a custom button and I want to see and set its text in the scene it's instantiated in. Currently I do this:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@export var text: String:\r\n\tset(value):\r\n\t\tif not is_node_ready():\r\n\t\t\tawait ready\r\n\t\tget_node(^\"MarginContainer/Text\").text = value\r\n\tget:\r\n\t\treturn get_node(^\"MarginContainer/Text\").text\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut I as far as I understand this will be highlighted as a warning with this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5601626435/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5602548037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321#issuecomment-5602548037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123321","id":5602548037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTfAZRQ","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:21:14Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T10:37:55Z","body":"That's exactly the pattern that sparked the discussion on this. If you accidentally do that in a `@tool` it corrupts you scenes on export (see the linked RC thread). The same corruption can also easily happen when your scene is used in a context you did not account for (e.g. removing from tree, setting text, then readding). It's very brittle code.\r\n\r\nThe solution is to always immediately use the backing field and then do side effects in a co-routine.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _update_label():\r\n    if not is_node_ready():\r\n        await ready\r\n    get_node(^\"MarginContainer/Text\").text = text\r\n\r\n@export var text: String:\r\n    set(value):\r\n        text = value\r\n        _update_label()\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlthough I'd personally recommend this instead since it's more robust in terms of the node lifecycle.\r\n```gdscript\r\n@onready var _label = $\"MarginContainer/Text\"\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n    _label.text = text\r\n\r\n@export var text: String:\r\n    set(value):\r\n        text = value\r\n        if is_instance_valid(_label):\r\n            _label.text = text\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5602548037/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5604451198","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321#issuecomment-5604451198","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123321","id":5604451198,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTg0jfg","user":{"login":"DexterFstone","id":92402263,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYHyVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92402263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone","html_url":"https://github.com/DexterFstone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T15:31:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T15:31:34Z","body":"> Although I'd personally recommend this instead since it's more robust in terms of the node lifecycle.\r\n> \r\n> ```gdscript\r\n> @onready var _label = $\"MarginContainer/Text\"\r\n> \r\n> func _update_label():\r\n>     if is_instance_valid(_label):\r\n>         _label.text = text\r\n> \r\n> @export var text: String:\r\n>     set(value):\r\n>         text = value\r\n>         _update_label()\r\n> \r\n> func _notification(what):\r\n>     if what == NOTIFICATION_READY or what == NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE:\r\n>         _update_label()\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nIt just increases the number of codes you need to write","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5604451198/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5888539159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123321#issuecomment-5888539159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123321","id":5888539159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXvv6Fw","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T10:39:32Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T10:40:29Z","body":"It not just increases code, it makes the code support the full `Node` lifecycle. If you care about encapsulation that's important. (Also note that I added a shorter lifecycle safe snippet to my last comment)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5888539159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]